# The Worldgorger Dragon loop with another creature card in a graveyard is no draw: it contains a choice (CR 104.4b). Bot2
# has Entombed an Ornithopter on turn 2. On turn 3 Bot1 animates the Dragon; its enters ability exiles Animate Dead and
# both Swamps (tapped for it), Animate Dead's leaves ability makes Bot1 sacrifice the Dragon, and the Dragon's leaves
# ability returns them all, new objects (CR 400.7), the Swamps untapped. Animate Dead, put onto the battlefield without
# being cast, chooses what it enchants (CR 303.4f, the Worldgorger Dragon ruling): a creature card in a graveyard, which is
# now the Dragon or Bot2's Ornithopter, and not targeting. Bot1 chooses the Dragon ten times, going round the loop ten
# times - far past the three rounds after which a loop of passes is a draw (RX-4), and still no draw, for each of those
# was a choice - and
# then the Ornithopter, so Animate Dead's enters ability
# returns it under Bot1's control (CR 110.2) and the loop is over: the Dragon stays in the graveyard, and Bot1 has two
# untapped Swamps again (mana made in the loop would have stayed in the pool all along, CR 106.4).

